            <ArticleTitle>Surgical repair of Wolff-Parkinson-White syndrome complicated with myocardial bridging.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>119-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myocardial bridging causes myocardial ischemia during supraventricular tachycardia. We present a case of Wolff-Parkinson-White syndrome combined with myocardial bridging. The patient complained of angina pectoris during paroxysmal supraventricular tachycardia because of severe constriction of the left anterior descending coronary artery during systole. A myocardial scintigram revealed myocardial ischemia in the anteroseptal wall during paroxysmal supraventricular tachycardia. Myotomy to prevent myocardial bridging and interruption of the accessory conduction pathway was successfully accomplished in a one-stage operation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
